## Comparison and exact-copy guard

If `measurement_text` presents a treated/control comparison, `vs`, `from ...
to ...`, percent change or inhibition, fold change, or a value defined relative
to another experimental group, return `relative` with `[]`. Do not extract one
absolute-looking component from that comparative string.

For `ok`, copy nonempty `unit_text` exactly, including every parenthetical and
qualifier. Never shorten it. Commas matching groups of three digits are
thousands separators, not decimal marks: `1,825` becomes `1825`, never `1.825`.
